se a higher card if he wants to beat it, possibly weakening him.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n- Playing ♣J retains ♥K as a potential winner later.  \n- If landlord passes (he has 3 cards, maybe no single higher than J), then my teammate gets the lead and may play out his cards.  \n- If landlord beats ♣J, he uses one of his few cards, and I still have ♥K to possibly regain control later.  \n- This move balances applying pressure with conserving strength.  \n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♣J"]}'}
